1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,540
In the 1690s,

2
00:00:01,540 --> 00:00:02,800
a girl named Jane told

3
00:00:02,800 --> 00:00:03,860
a court about the night

4
00:00:03,860 --> 00:00:05,640
her mother was killed.

5
00:00:05,640 --> 00:00:06,280
She said they had

6
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:07,180
just woken from

7
00:00:07,180 --> 00:00:09,100
their “first sleep.”

8
00:00:09,100 --> 00:00:10,280
Centuries later,

9
00:00:10,280 --> 00:00:11,480
a historian read that,

10
00:00:11,480 --> 00:00:13,120
and stopped.

11
00:00:13,120 --> 00:00:14,160
First sleep?

12
00:00:14,160 --> 00:00:14,600
Then what was

13
00:00:14,600 --> 00:00:15,720
the second?

14
00:00:15,720 --> 00:00:16,460
He found both

15
00:00:16,460 --> 00:00:17,700
in diaries,

16
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,660
plays and doctors'

17
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:19,460
books.

18
00:00:19,460 --> 00:00:20,000
About two

19
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:21,640
thousand times.

20
00:00:21,640 --> 00:00:22,780
Many Europeans once

21
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:24,140
slept twice a night,

22
00:00:24,140 --> 00:00:25,080
with an hour or so

23
00:00:25,080 --> 00:00:26,620
awake around midnight.

24
00:00:26,620 --> 00:00:27,620
In that hour,

25
00:00:27,620 --> 00:00:28,660
people prayed,

26
00:00:28,660 --> 00:00:29,340
talked,

27
00:00:29,340 --> 00:00:29,660
or visited

28
00:00:29,660 --> 00:00:30,820
the neighbours.

29
00:00:30,820 --> 00:00:31,280
But as lamps

30
00:00:31,280 --> 00:00:32,340
got brighter,

31
00:00:32,340 --> 00:00:32,960
the two sleeps

32
00:00:32,960 --> 00:00:34,060
became one,

33
00:00:34,060 --> 00:00:34,600
and the phrase

34
00:00:34,600 --> 00:00:35,860
was forgotten.

35
00:00:35,860 --> 00:00:37,510
In one experiment,

36
00:00:37,520 --> 00:00:37,840
volunteers kept

37
00:00:37,840 --> 00:00:38,980
in darkness fourteen

38
00:00:38,980 --> 00:00:40,200
hours a night began

39
00:00:40,200 --> 00:00:42,310
sleeping in two halves.

40
00:00:42,720 --> 00:00:43,160
Researchers still

41
00:00:43,160 --> 00:00:44,260
debate how common

42
00:00:44,260 --> 00:00:45,900
two sleeps were.

43
00:00:45,900 --> 00:00:47,120
Jane never explained what

44
00:00:47,120 --> 00:00:49,000
“first sleep” meant.

45
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:50,360
She didn't need to.

46
00:00:50,360 --> 00:00:51,140
Back then,

47
00:00:51,140 --> 00:00:52,500
everyone knew.
